Ladybird creates the srcdoc parser with the encoding used to produce
its response body. Blink passes UTF-8 to FillStaticResponse in
RenderFrameImpl. WebKit supplies UTF-8 in the ResourceResponse from
FrameLoader::defaultSubstituteDataForURL. Gecko converts the supplied
string to UTF-8 and sets the channel charset in
NS_NewInputStreamChannelInternal.

Chrome 158.0.8127.38, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 preserved the
apostrophe, euro sign, and emoji with no declaration, a UTF-8
declaration, and a conflicting windows-1252 declaration.
